<title>ESTONIA: Estonia banks sign deal with Paribas Belgium. [CORRECTED 13:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Estonia banks sign deal with Paribas Belgium. [CORRECTED 13:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Estonian banks, Eesti Uhispank and  Tallinnapank, have signed a deal for a 150 million Belgian franc export credit agreement with Bank Paribas Belgium, Uhispank said on Monday.</p>
<p>Uhispank's share of the deal is 100 million francs and Tallinnapank's is 50 million francs, Uhispank added.</p>
<p>&quot;This credit is aimed at financing imports from Belgium to Estonia,&quot; Uhispank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The sum that can be lent ranges from a minimum three million francs to a maximum 100 million francs. The Estonian importer has to fund 15 percent (corrects from &quot;50 percent&quot;) of the deal from its own funds.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom +371 7 22 66 93</p>
</text>
